  "review_state": "reviewed",
  "contract": "A child's resolution while its parent has a ready workflow task (published Server 2.11.7 with Workflow 2.15.7 WorkflowExecutor::dispatchParentResumeTasks), over raw worker HTTP on protocol 1.20 in a fresh namespace. The parent's first task starts a child on its own queue and schedules an activity; the activity's result leaves the parent a ready resume task; then the child completes. The resolution is recorded and the ready task, unchanged, is the parent's only resume: a worker can claim exactly one parent task, with no update id, whose history carries ChildRunCompleted, and completing it closes the run. Embedded applications have no worker protocol.",
